Introduction
The Security Operations Center (SOC) is a central hub for securing many large organizations, and junior analysts are among the most numerous and demanding roles in a SOC. In the analyst role, you will work with logs, triage and prioritize alerts, collaborate with your teammates and other departments, and be the first line of defense in reacting to cyber incidents. This comprehensive path covers the necessary technical and operational skills to make you a qualified, universal SOC analyst.

What Is a Security Analyst?
New threats show up constantly in cyber security, and it only takes one bad click to let an attacker in. Somebody has to be watching for that. A security analyst monitors the activity taking place within the organisation's systems for anything untoward. The security analyst investigates and determines if there is malicious activity taking place, and reports it to their wider team.
A normal shift might start with a scroll through the security news. There's usually something in there; a big company got breached, a group is running a fresh campaign, a new vulnerability just got announced. Staying aware of it all is part of the job, because you're the one keeping your own company off that list.
